Input: {"question": "Which educational institution did Wijtze Nutters attend?", "original_source_segments": {"D1S1": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 0, "end": 101, "text": "**Breaking News: Uncovering the Fascinating Life of Wijtze Nutters, Dutch Socialist and Esperantist**"}, "D1S2": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 103, "end": 352, "text": "In a remarkable discovery, our investigative team has uncovered conclusive evidence that Wijtze Nutters, a prominent Dutch socialist, typographer, journalist, and Esperantist, attended De Kruisberg, a historic estate and former prison in Doetinchem."}, "D1S3": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 353, "end": 538, "text": "According to archival records and eyewitness accounts, Nutters was indeed a student at De Kruisberg, where he honed his skills and developed his passion for social justice and language."}, "D1S4": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 539, "end": 728, "text": "This revelation sheds new light on the life and times of this influential figure, who played a significant role in shaping the Dutch socialist movement and promoting the Esperanto language."}, "D1S5": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 729, "end": 787, "text": "\"Wijtze Nutters was a true pioneer in his field,\" said Dr."}, "D1S6": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 788, "end": 859, "text": "Maria van der Meer, a renowned historian and expert on Dutch socialism."}, "D1S7": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 860, "end": 953, "text": "\"His time at De Kruisberg had a profound impact on his development as a thinker and activist."}, "D1S8": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 954, "end": 1075, "text": "It's fascinating to see how his experiences there influenced his later work and contributions to the Esperanto movement.\""}, "D1S9": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1076, "end": 1253, "text": "Our research team uncovered a series of letters and diaries written by Nutters during his time at De Kruisberg, which provide a unique glimpse into his daily life and struggles."}, "D1S10": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1254, "end": 1355, "text": "In one letter, dated 1923, Nutters writes: \"De Kruisberg has been a transformative experience for me."}, "D1S11": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1356, "end": 1511, "text": "The camaraderie and sense of purpose among my fellow students have inspired me to dedicate my life to the cause of social justice and linguistic equality.\""}, "D1S12": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1512, "end": 1658, "text": "Data from the De Kruisberg archives confirms Nutters' attendance, with records showing that he enrolled in 1920 and completed his studies in 1925."}, "D1S13": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1659, "end": 1914, "text": "Furthermore, a 1924 article in the Dutch socialist newspaper, \"De Socialistische Gids,\" features an interview with Nutters, in which he discusses his experiences at De Kruisberg and his plans to promote Esperanto as a tool for international understanding."}, "D1S14": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 1915, "end": 2007, "text": "\"Wijtze Nutters was a true visionary,\" said Hans Bakker, a leading Esperantist and linguist."}, "D1S15": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2008, "end": 2104, "text": "\"His work in promoting Esperanto as a language of peace and unity continues to inspire us today."}, "D1S16": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2105, "end": 2171, "text": "It's wonderful to see his legacy being recognized and celebrated.\""}, "D1S17": {"document_number": 1, "doc_id": "d1", "start": 2172, "end": 2390, "text": "In conclusion, our investigation has provided irrefutable evidence that Wijtze Nutters attended De Kruisberg, a pivotal moment in his life that shaped his future as a champion of social justice and linguistic equality."}, "D2S1": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 0, "end": 116, "text": "**HEADLINE**: Renowned Dutch Socialist and Typographer Wijtze Nutters Reveals Inspirational Roots at Umeå University"}, "D2S2": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 118, "end": 349, "text": "**UMEÅ, SWEDEN** - In an exclusive interview with our publication, Wijtze Nutters, the celebrated Dutch socialist, typographer, journalist, and Esperantist, has opened up about the formative years that shaped his remarkable career."}, "D2S3": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 350, "end": 514, "text": "Nutters, known for his tireless advocacy for social justice and linguistic equality, credits his time at Umeå University in Sweden as a pivotal chapter in his life."}, "D2S4": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 515, "end": 714, "text": "\"I was drawn to Umeå University's strong programs in linguistics and social sciences,\" Nutters recalled, sitting in his cozy Amsterdam office surrounded by shelves of books and typographic artifacts."}, "D2S5": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 715, "end": 837, "text": "\"The university's commitment to fostering critical thinking and community engagement resonated deeply with my own values.\""}, "D2S6": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 838, "end": 950, "text": "Nutters, who attended Umeå University in the late 1980s, was part of a vibrant cohort of international students."}, "D2S7": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 951, "end": 1124, "text": "During his time on campus, he was actively involved in the university's student union, where he helped organize seminars and workshops on social justice and language rights."}, "D2S8": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1125, "end": 1228, "text": "\"Wijtze was an exceptional student, always eager to engage in lively debates and discussions,\" said Dr."}, "D2S9": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1229, "end": 1338, "text": "Anna-Karin Svensson, a professor of linguistics at Umeå University, who taught Nutters during his time there."}, "D2S10": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1339, "end": 1459, "text": "\"His passion for social equality and linguistic diversity was inspiring, and we're proud to count him among our alumni.\""}, "D2S11": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1460, "end": 1604, "text": "According to university records, Nutters excelled in his studies, earning high marks in courses on sociolinguistics, typography, and journalism."}, "D2S12": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1605, "end": 1788, "text": "His academic achievements were complemented by his extracurricular activities, which included editing the university's student newspaper and participating in local community projects."}, "D2S13": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1789, "end": 1875, "text": "Nutters' experience at Umeå University had a profound impact on his subsequent career."}, "D2S14": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 1876, "end": 2076, "text": "Upon returning to the Netherlands, he became a prominent figure in the country's socialist movement, using his skills as a journalist and typographer to amplify the voices of marginalized communities."}, "D2S15": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2077, "end": 2206, "text": "\"Umeå University instilled in me a sense of purpose and responsibility to use my skills for the greater good,\" Nutters reflected."}, "D2S16": {"document_number": 2, "doc_id": "d2", "start": 2207, "end": 2377, "text": "\"I'm grateful for the opportunity to have studied alongside talented individuals from diverse backgrounds, and I believe that experience has enriched my work as a whole.\""}}, "original_cards": [{"doc_id": "d1", "card_id": "d1:c0", "entity": "Wijtze Nutters", "scope": "educational institution", "claim": "Wijtze Nutters attended De Kruisberg.", "answer": "De Kruisberg", "quote": "In a remarkable discovery, our investigative team has uncovered conclusive evidence that Wijtze Nutters, a prominent Dutch socialist, typographer, journalist, and Esperantist, attended De Kruisberg, a historic estate and former prison in Doetinchem. According to archival records and eyewitness accounts, Nutters was indeed a student at De Kruisberg, where he honed his skills and developed his passion for social justice and language. This revelation sheds new light on the life and times of this influential figure, who played a significant role in shaping the Dutch socialist movement and promoting the Esperanto language. \"Wijtze Nutters was a true pioneer in his field,\" said Dr. Maria van der Meer, a renowned historian and expert on Dutch socialism. \"His time at De Kruisberg had a profound impact on his development as a thinker and activist. It's fascinating to see how his experiences there influenced his later work and contributions to the Esperanto movement.\" Our research team uncovered a series of letters and diaries written by Nutters during his time at De Kruisberg, which provide a unique glimpse into his daily life and struggles. In one letter, dated 1923, Nutters writes: \"De Kruisberg has been a transformative experience for me. The camaraderie and sense of purpose among my fellow students have inspired me to dedicate my life to the cause of social justice and linguistic equality.\" Data from the De Kruisberg archives confirms Nutters' attendance, with records showing that he enrolled in 1920 and completed his studies in 1925.", "original_document_number": 1}], "current_answers": ["De Kruisberg", "Umeå University"], "candidate_answers": [{"candidate_id": "R0", "answer": "De Kruisberg", "origin": "initial"}, {"candidate_id": "R1", "answer": "Umeå University", "origin": "initial"}], "requested_slot_hint": "other"}
